cannot be instantiated at `i64`

`Nautilus.LinAlg` is generic over one `prec: Float` binder per function, and
that bound admits float dtypes only ([04-DTYPE-2]). An integer matrix passed to
`det_2x2` must be rejected at the bound, not by an arithmetic failure deeper in
the body.

The pinned diagnostic changed with the conversion, and the new one is stronger.
The f32-only signature rejected this as `tensor precision mismatch: f32 vs i64`
-- true, but a statement about one concrete declared dtype, which a caller could
have read as "LinAlg happens to be f32 today". The bound rejection is a
statement about the contract: no integer dtype is admissible at any
instantiation. It also discriminates, where the old text did not: the
pre-generic module produces the old diagnostic for this same file, so this
`.expect` cannot pass against it.
